><surname>Vergona</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Wheeler</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Morgan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Schlesselman</surname><given-names>JJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors related to inflammation of the ovarian epithelium and risk of ovarian cancer</article-title><source>Epidemiology</source><year>2000</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>111</fpage><lpage>117</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11021606</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00001648-200003000-00006</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rae</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Niven</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Critchley</surname><given-names>HO</given-names></name><name><surname>Harlow</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Hillier</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Antiinflammatory steroid action in human ovarian surface epithelial cells</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><year>2004</year><volume>89</volume><fpage>4538</fpage><lpage>4544</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15356059</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1210/jc.2003-032225</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Balkwill</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Coussens</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cancer: an inflammatory link</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2004</year><volume>431</volume><fpage>405</fpage><lpage>406</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15385993</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/431405a</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name